  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Crlr/633/2025 on 25 September, 2025",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "It is the contended by learned counsel for the revisionist that in Section 63 of the said Act, an amendment has been brought about by amending Act \"The Jan Vishwas (Amendment of Provisions) 2023\", whereby, punishment \"with imprisonment for a term may be extend to six months and also with a fine, which may extend to Rs.5,00,000/-\" has been amended to \"liable to penalty which may extend to Rs.10,00,000/-\". 6. Learned counsel for the revisionist submits that since amendment has been brought about w.e.f. 11.08.2023, punishment of one month cannot be inflicted upon the revisionist and he can only be inflicted with a fine up to Rs.10,00,000/- for the reason that the amendment is beneficial to the CRLR/633/2025 on 25 September, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/24501285/ 1 accused/ revisionist, even if the incident happened prior the date of amendment.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is the contended by learned counsel for the revisionist that in Section 63 of the said Act, an amendment has been brought about by amending Act \"The Jan Vishwas (Amendment of Provisions) 2023\", whereby, punishment \"with imprisonment for a term may be extend to six months and also with a fine, which may extend to Rs.5,00,000/-\" has been amended to \"liable to penalty which may extend to Rs.10,00,000/-\". 6. Learned counsel for the revisionist submits that since amendment has been brought about w.e.f. 11.08.2023, punishment of one month cannot be inflicted upon the revisionist and he can only be inflicted with a fine up to Rs.10,00,000/- for the reason that the amendment is beneficial to the CRLR/633/2025 on 25 September, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/24501285/ 1 accused/ revisionist, even if the incident happened prior the date of amendment.",
